      "sample_index": 2,
      "text": "First we note that, any even power of $11$ is a palindrome. So, we only need to examine odd powers. Here are the first few powers of $11$:\n\\begin{align}\n11^1 &= 11 \\\\\n11^3 &= 1331 \\\\\n11^5 &= 161051 \\\\\n11^7 &= 19487171 \\\\\n11^9 &= 2357947691\n\\end{align}\n(The actual powers I had to think of were $1$, $5$, $7$, and $9$.)\n\nAny power of $11$ that is greater than $1$ (since $11^1 = 11$ is a palindrome, but $19487171$ is not) will be really close to being a palindrome, like $11^7 = 19487171$, which is just over a $2$ decimal place from being a palindrome. We want the smallest integer power of $11$, which is $\\boxed{11}$.\nThe answer is: 11",
